# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} manifest — schema

> ⛔ **TODO — SCHEMA DOC, NOT THE MANIFEST ITSELF.** This file documents the shape of the
> per-version manifest JSON (`manifest/manifest-{{DS_VERSION}}.json`). It does NOT
> contain real {{SYSTEM_NAME}} data.
>
> **To start:** copy the skeleton at the bottom into `manifest/manifest-{{DS_VERSION}}.json`,
> fill `summary` from `tools/inventory-snippet.js`, seed `keyTokens` / `keyComponents` with your
> load-bearing tokens + components, and append a `patches[]` entry on every published change. See
> `manifest/baseline.example.json` for a tiny, concrete, valid instance.
>
> The manifest is **curated ground truth** — it does not enumerate every variable/component, only the
> counts + the key tokens/components + the change history. `tools/doc-drift-checker.py` validates it
> against a live inventory.

The manifest is the single curated record of "what {{SYSTEM_NAME}} is at version X and how it got
there." One file per published version. The drift checker (`tools/doc-drift-checker.py`) asserts the
`summary` counts, `keyTokens`, and `keyComponents` against a live `inventory-snippet.js` dump.

---

## Top-level fields

| Field | Type | Required | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `version` | string | ✅ | the published version, e.g. `"{{DS_VERSION}}"` |
| `publishedAt` | string (date) | ✅ | ISO date this version was published |
| `lastPatchedAt` | string (date) | ✅ | ISO date of the most recent `patches[]` entry |
| `patches` | array&lt;Patch&gt; | ✅ | reverse-chronological change log (newest first) |
| `summary` | Summary | ✅ | the counts the drift checker validates |
| `collections` | array&lt;Collection&gt; | ✅ | variable collections + per-collection counts |
| `keyTokens` | object&lt;name → "VariableID:.."&gt; | ✅ | load-bearing tokens, validated by ID + name |
| `keyComponents` | object&lt;label → publishedKey&gt; | ✅ | load-bearing components, validated by key |
| `knownGaps` | array&lt;string&gt; | ✅ | documented gaps + their interim workarounds |
| `<version>_changes` | object | optional | rich detail on the headline additions this version (e.g. `keyComponents` with full prop definitions) |
| `gotchas_added_*` / `carryover_from_*` | optional | optional | narrative notes carried across versions |

### Patch (one entry per published change)

| Field | Type | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `date` | string (date) | when the change landed |
| `scope` | string | one-line summary of WHAT changed (component/token + version) |
| `change` | string | the full technical detail — IDs, keys, before/after values, rationale |
| `republished` | boolean | whether this change has been published to consumers |
| `consumerImpact` | string | breaking vs non-breaking, what consumers must do (e.g. swap stale instances) |
| `documentedAs` | string | where else this is recorded (skills, CLAUDE.md, knownGaps) |
| `qa` | string | how it was verified (render-verify, binding audit, contrast recompute) |
| `tokenChange` | object | optional — structured `{ token, id, from, to }` for a token re-alias |

### Summary (drift-checked counts)

```json
{
  "variableCount": 0,
  "textStyleCount": 0,
  "effectStyleCount": 0,
  "componentSetCount": 0,
  "iconCount": 0,
  "illustrationCount": 0
}
```

`componentSetCount` is the curated count of DOCUMENTED UI sets — the drift checker treats it as
**informational**, not drift (the live file also contains icon/illustration sets).

### Collection

```json
{ "name": "1. Primitives", "id": "VariableCollectionId:__:_", "variableCount": 0, "modes": ["Value"] }
```

### keyTokens / keyComponents (the validated maps)

- `keyTokens` — `{ "Surface/Page": "VariableID:__:_", ... }`. The value may carry a trailing annotation
  (`"VariableID:24:88 (4px)"`); the checker reads only the bare `VariableID:` prefix. Each is validated
  by **both** its VariableID and its name against the live file.
- `keyComponents` — `{ "Status Bar / Style=Light": "<40-hex-key>", ... }`. Each key must resolve against
  every live component + variant key.

### knownGaps

A flat array of strings, each a gap + its workaround (and resolution note once closed). Example:
`"Body/Default-Bold style still missing — workaround: inline SemiBold override"`.

---

## Minimal {{DS_VERSION}} skeleton

Copy this into `manifest/manifest-{{DS_VERSION}}.json` and fill it in:

```json
{
  "version": "{{DS_VERSION}}",
  "publishedAt": "{{DS_PUBLISHED_DATE}}",
  "lastPatchedAt": "{{DS_PUBLISHED_DATE}}",
  "patches": [],
  "summary": {
    "variableCount": 0,
    "textStyleCount": 0,
    "effectStyleCount": 0,
    "componentSetCount": 0,
    "iconCount": 0,
    "illustrationCount": 0
  },
  "collections": [
    { "name": "1. Primitives", "id": "VariableCollectionId:__:_", "variableCount": 0, "modes": ["Value"] },
    { "name": "2. Tokens",     "id": "VariableCollectionId:__:_", "variableCount": 0, "modes": ["Value"] },
    { "name": "3. Semantic",   "id": "VariableCollectionId:__:_", "variableCount": 0, "modes": ["Light"] }
  ],
  "keyTokens": {},
  "keyComponents": {},
  "knownGaps": []
}
```
